From 411775f42a73da4ecbc8643c6145c783a1aa8b65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ohos-kernel-port contributors <232252@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 08:29:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mm: pass both arguments to PAGEFLAG_FALSE for two page flags

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only

Baseline: gitcode.com/openharmony/kernel_linux_6.6
Branch:   OpenHarmony-7.0-Release
Commit:   f4b61510491aa20f7f57fbbc5efc754083c92212

    include/linux/page-flags.h:519:27: error: macro "PAGEFLAG_FALSE"
        requires 2 arguments, but only 1 given
      519 | PAGEFLAG_FALSE(XPMReadonly)
    include/linux/page-flags.h:520:31: error: macro "PAGEFLAG_FALSE"
        requires 2 arguments, but only 1 given
      520 | PAGEFLAG_FALSE(XPMWritetainted)
    include/linux/page-flags.h:519:1: error: unknown type name 'PAGEFLAG_FALSE'
    include/linux/page-flags.h:520:15: error: expected ';' before 'static'

PAGEFLAG_FALSE takes (uname, lname), and every other call site in the file
passes both.  The #ifdef branch three lines above uses
PAGEFLAG(XPMReadonly, xpm_readonly, PF_HEAD), and two lines above the second
one PAGEFLAG_FALSE(VmemmapSelfHosted, vmemmap_self_hosted) is correct.  The
preprocessor does not expand a call with the wrong arity, so the token is left
where a declaration belongs and the errors cascade.

There is a second instance of the same mistake, further down, which the
compiler had not reached when the first one stopped the build:

    include/linux/page-flags.h:660: PAGEFLAG_FALSE(Purgeable)

under CONFIG_MEM_PURGEABLE, whose #ifdef branch is
PAGEFLAG(Purgeable, purgeable, PF_ANY).  Both are fixed here so the #else
branches compile in any configuration.  kernel_linux_config's
type/standard_defconfig and the rk3568 board configuration do set
CONFIG_MEM_PURGEABLE, so the Purgeable one is reachable in practice.

The lower-case names are the ones the corresponding #ifdef branches already use
for the same flags, so the two branches stay consistent.

Upstream: no equivalent; these lines are not part of Linux v6.6.
Licence: GPL-2.0-only, same as the tree.
---
 include/linux/page-flags.h | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/linux/page-flags.h b/include/linux/page-flags.h
index aa37e68..c4069e8 100644
--- a/include/linux/page-flags.h
+++ b/include/linux/page-flags.h
@@ -516,8 +516,8 @@ PAGEFLAG(Checked, checked, PF_NO_COMPOUND)	   /* Used by some filesystems */
 PAGEFLAG(XPMReadonly, xpm_readonly, PF_HEAD)
 PAGEFLAG(XPMWritetainted, xpm_writetainted, PF_HEAD)
 #else
-PAGEFLAG_FALSE(XPMReadonly)
-PAGEFLAG_FALSE(XPMWritetainted)
+PAGEFLAG_FALSE(XPMReadonly, xpm_readonly)
+PAGEFLAG_FALSE(XPMWritetainted, xpm_writetainted)
 #endif
 
 /* Xen */
@@ -657,7 +657,7 @@ PAGEFLAG_FALSE(VmemmapSelfHosted, vmemmap_self_hosted)
 #ifdef CONFIG_MEM_PURGEABLE
 PAGEFLAG(Purgeable, purgeable, PF_ANY)
 #else
-PAGEFLAG_FALSE(Purgeable)
+PAGEFLAG_FALSE(Purgeable, purgeable)
 #endif
 
 /*
-- 
